{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact d2704473a126932f70240f20870a265fb2180dfd. Fresh root gates pass, but six independently reproduced admission defects prevent approval. Builder's reported repairs at 22ee206d are not yet submitted or independently approved. Preserve the following failures and their passing controls in the replacement evidence.\n\n1. P1 — Keep an invitation's v2-era default authority when redeeming after v2→v1 activation. packages/room/src/requests.ts:243 defaults an absent session to \"*\"; under v1 admission expands that to every delegable role kind. A room-custody invitation issued under v2 with no session, originally renew-only (R-DECL-17), redeemed after v1 activation produced claim, propose, note, review, land, release and renew permission. Its bearer successfully opened a claim. Preserve the issuing vocabulary/default through storage and upgrades; do not acquire legacy wildcard authority.\n\n2. P1 — Recheck current who.delegable when a delegated act is used. packages/room/src/authority.ts:153-174 checks the stored signed map, binding and current role but omits current delegability. Grant claim while delegable, activate only who.delegable=false, and submit a fresh delegated claim: it is accepted and advances the sequence. The binding correctly remains equal because who is excluded from meaning identity (R-DECL-15). R-DECL-11 and amended R-ADM-5 still require current delegation restrictions at use. Refuse delegation-invalid without recording; retain the before-change passing control.\n\n3. P2 — Return an accepted exact retry before current target/vocabulary shape rejection. packages/room/src/admission.ts:224,316 checks the current declaration before the idempotency lookup at 320; schema.ts:187-199 validates its current targets. An accepted entry-anchored note, retried byte-identically after a valid policy change removes that target, throws bad-request (\"envelope.target.act is not a field of this type.\") instead of its original receipt. The unchanged-declaration control passes. Preserve R-DECL-16/R-IDEM exact receipts across meaning and format changes, while still authenticating the original signature and rejecting changed bytes/signatures.\n\n4. P2 — Keep application body.purpose out of legacy recovery dispatch. Declared-body validation permits a user-defined purpose field (schema.ts:430-436); dispatch forwards it to claimNew (admission.ts:618,788,797-809). With a valid optional purpose enum and an active block-claim rule, purpose=ordinary is refused but purpose=config-recovery opens a flagged recovery thread under an admin's own key, bypassing the rule. This is an admin policy bypass, not a lower-role escalation. Under R-DECL-21 only platform recover creates recovery behavior. Strip/translate application fields before legacy adapters or otherwise isolate platform semantics; keep both paired assertions.\n\n5. P2 — Refuse stale mapped invitations atomically across v2→v1. requests.ts:243 drops a v2 invitation's signed session map under a current v1 document, and 301 issues a legacy grant. A signed claim binding plus renew map was redeemed/consumed after v1 activation; keys/grant/sequence were created and the map became null. R-DECL-17 explicitly requires binding-stale at redemption, with current policy/version metadata, an unused invitation and no key/grant/log changes. Grant admission's kind-undeclared case is distinct. Do not invent an absent current binding or silently downgrade the map.\n\n6. P2 — Read declared body fields as own properties. schema.ts:433 tests b[name]!==undefined, so valid optional text field toString is validated against Object.prototype.toString when omitted. Explicit text passes; omission fails invalid-body (\"body.toString must be a string.\"). Valid optional fields must be absent when not owned; required inherited-name fields must still be required. The constructor hypothesis was discarded because the profile forbids that name. The bool goal collision probe passed